# NOTE: GitHub Pages does not read this file at all -- it has no support for
# custom response headers. These headers only take effect once the domain is
# proxied through Cloudflare with a Transform Rule (see worker/README.md).
# Keep this file accurate anyway: it's the source of truth for what the rule should say.
#
# Until then, every page carries the same Content-Security-Policy and
# Referrer-Policy as <meta> tags (scripts/set-security-meta.py). Keep the two
# policies in step. The header version adds frame-ancestors, which a <meta>
# tag cannot set.
#
# No page has an inline <script> that runs code any more (October 2026), so
# script-src needs no hashes. Keep it that way: put new scripts in /assets/*.js.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.workers.dev https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
